				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1606633#post-2507353</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1606633/date-night#post-2507353</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 12 May 2016 02:06:20 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Hercules Rockefeller</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2314402</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Same here, it's the underlying darkness that first attracted me to lolFoundation, and what I love the most about it. A lot of people dismiss the canon because they confuse it with the lolFoundation era of the site (which is a whole other thing, and one that I personally dislike), or because they don't stop to look past the silliness. But when you actually read the &quot;rules&quot; of lolFoundation on the canon hub, it becomes clear that the canon is a lot darker than it first seems - in many ways, lolFoundation is the darkest canon on the site: there's no point to anything, no escape. Even Competitive Eschatology has hope - this doesn't.</p> <p>It was reading that hub page that really hooked me to the canon and inspired me to write this tale, as well as the follow-up tale I'm currently working on (and which, incidentally, will be significantly darker than this first one).</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
